From 001c4f2f6321b5bb07d73adfb268986d92823e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:11:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stop nurse/caretaker signups from becoming PATIENT
 accounts

/auth/send-otp created User(role=PATIENT) + PatientProfile as soon as an OTP
was requested, so anyone who tapped Send OTP before using
'Apply as a caregiver' was permanently a patient and /nurse/self-signup then
failed with 'already registered as PATIENT'.

- send-otp no longer creates a user; the session is parked in PendingOTP and
  the PATIENT user is created only after a successful verify-otp
- verify-otp self-heals legacy records and persists the FCM device token
- nurse self-signup converts an empty auto-created PATIENT shell into a NURSE
- VerifyOTPRequest.token is optional
- admin nurse approve also activates the user
- scripts/fix_nurse_patient_roles.py cleans up existing bad data
